  "root_cause": "Forensic root cause identified: In the authoritative Population-U atlas generator (run_unconditioned_atlas_engine.py), when a new pullback episode initialized (gb_atr >= 0.50), it contained an immediate multi-milestone emission clause for PB1.00 (if gb_atr >= 1.00: emit PB1.00), but lacked initial-bar emission clauses for PB1.50 or PB2.00 on that same first bar (those were only checked on continuation bars). In run_gate1_streaming_parity.py, the streaming author anticipated large 5s gap bars and added initialization checks for PB1.50 and PB2.00 (lines 304-315). In January 2023, exactly 6 episodes experienced a fast 5s impulse that jumped directly from <0.50 ATR to >=1.50 ATR (and in one case >=2.00 ATR) on the very first 5s bar, causing run_gate1 to emit 7 extra multi-milestone initial-bar records (6 x PB1.50, 1 x PB2.00). All 6,641 authoritative records matched with zero error (0.00e+00). This is a benign single-bar multi-milestone gap emission difference in the parity test harness, not a runtime population semantics mismatch.",
